    <string name="setup_title">Setup guide</string>
    <string name="setup_why">AutoComp attaches an audio effect to the sessions of other apps. Android only allows that with elevated privileges, which Shizuku provides without root.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_install">1. Install Shizuku (from its GitHub releases or Google Play).</string>
    <string name="setup_step_start_11">2. Open Shizuku and start it with Wireless debugging (Android 11+): enable Developer options, turn on Wireless debugging, pair, then tap Start.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_start_old">2. Open Shizuku and follow its instructions to start it with a USB cable and ADB (Android 9–10).</string>
    <string name="setup_step_grant">3. Come back here and grant AutoComp access to Shizuku.</string>
    <string name="setup_step_reboot">Shizuku has to be started again after each reboot unless you use root or Android 11+ wireless debugging auto-start.</string>
    <string name="setup_privacy">AutoComp has no network access and collects nothing.</string>
